# by F.C.
#
# Ebuilds from my local repo.

# Ryzen >= 5000 (Zen3) termal sensor and monitoring (emerge zenmonitor3
# with zenpower 3 or 5) + NCT6687-R Super I/O for MSI B550 Gaming Plus.
# Note: 'zenpower3' supports up to Zen3, while 'zenpower5' includes also
# support for some Zen4 and Zen5 CPUs (but not all yet). Both seem to work
# with kernels > 6.12 LTS and KDE/PLASMA System Monitor plasmoids. Instead
# 'k10temp' (now compatible with Ryzen >= 5000) does not work in plasmoids
# because it doesn't report the max CPU temperature. To use 'zenpower*',
# 'k10temp' must be blacklisted (see /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist.conf).
app-admin/zenmonitor3::local **
sys-kernel/zenpower5::local **
sys-kernel/zenpower3::local **
sys-kernel/nct6687d::local **

# Qt/C++ GUI front end to Fscrypt, Securefs, Ecryptfs, Cryfs, Encfs,
# Gocryptfs, Sshfs and Cryptomator (from holgersson overlay). It works
# perfectly with GoCryptFS >= 2.6-r1 from portage (i.e. stable version).
app-crypt/sirikali::local

# Plugin for OBS Studio, useful to remove or blur the background
# of captured images and videos (based on a neural network). See:
# https://github.com/occ-ai/obs-backgroundremoval
media-plugins/obs-backgroundremoval::local

# Programmer for TinyFPGA board (see also sci-electronics/openfpgaloader
# in /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/00-other_repos.accept_keywords).
# NOTE: The ebuilds of Icarus Verilog, Verilator, Yosys, iCEstorm, PrjTrellis,
# Apicula, and NextPNR have been removed from the local repo due to the high
# maintenance and testing workload. These tools are interrelated, and sometimes
# issues arise when updated individually. Instead, the OSS-CAD-SUITE environment
# (see https://github.com/YosysHQ/oss-cad-suite-build), is recommended because
# it offers a comprehensive all-in-one solution that works seamlessly on Gentoo
# (as well as on other Linux x86_64/Arm64 distributions, MacOS, and Windows);
# we can even have multiple versions of the OSS-CAD-SUITE installed.
sci-electronics/tinyprog::local
=dev-python/jsonmerge-1.9*::gentoo

# Electronic circuit simulator (browser based) with lot of examples.
sci-electronics/circuitjs1-bin::local

# Electronic circuit simulator.
sci-electronics/qucs-s::local

# Ellama is a friendly interface to Ollama.
# Run LLMs locally: Llama 3, Mistral, Gemma, DeepSeek-R1, ...
# NOTE: a high-end AMD or NVidia GPU is required. See docs in
# https://github.com/ollama/ollama, https://itsfoss.com/ollama/
# and https://itsfoss.com/install-deepseek-r1-locally-linux/
#
# There are also an updated ebuild "app-misc/ollama-bin" in:
# https://gpo.zugaina.org/Overlays/arrans-overlay/app-misc/ollama-bin
app-misc/ellama::local
acct-group/ollama::local
acct-user/ollama::local
dev-python/ollama::local
sci-ml/ollama::local

# NumPy-compatible array library accelerated by CUDA or ROCm.
dev-python/cupy::local
dev-python/fastrlock::local

# Clazy with latest fixes (see the ebuild).
dev-util/clazy::local

# Blender in portage is too old; also Python 11 has been disabled
# from PYTHON_COMPAT, so the stable ebuild currently fails. This
# ebuild fix it and bump blender to the latest LTS version. See:
# https://bugs.gentoo.org/973408, https://bugs.gentoo.org/976618
media-gfx/blender::local
